{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "01 — One command, end to end",
  "description": "Follow `init` and `add` from the shell into the files they write. Seventeen stops, in the order the code runs. Every stop carries a `pattern`: the text it expects on the line it cites, which `npm test` checks.",
  "ref": "main",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "bin/init.mjs",
      "line": 354,
      "pattern": "if \\(cmd === \"init\"\\) await init\\(\\);",
      "title": "The whole router",
      "description": "Start here. A command-line tool has no framework in front of it — the first word after the program name IS the route, and this if/else chain is the entire routing table.\n\nFive verbs. `npx @homenshum/easier-to-read-submissions init` and `node bin/init.mjs init` reach this same line, because package.json maps two binary names to this one file. `npx easier` does not: that word is somebody else's package on npm."
    },
    {
      "file": "bin/init.mjs",
      "line": 42,
      "pattern": "const args = process\\.argv\\.slice\\(2\\);",
      "title": "The only input this program has",
      "description": "Command arguments select the action. The CLI also reads the local filesystem and, for installation, the documented profile-directory environment variables. No provider credential or network request is required."
    },
    {
      "file": "bin/init.mjs",
      "line": 56,
      "pattern": "const INVOKE = ",
      "title": "How it tells you to run it again",
      "description": "The program prints the scoped package invocation when it runs from node_modules and a quoted source path when it runs from a checkout. A path containing spaces must be exercised by copy/pasting the displayed command, separately from direct argv tests. Windows shell evidence does not establish arbitrary-shell compatibility."
    },
    {
      "file": "bin/init.mjs",
      "line": 97,
      "pattern": "async function init\\(\\)",
      "title": "The primary user action",
      "description": "`init` is the moment a repository adopts the protocol. Somebody is about to hand a branch to a reviewer and wants a per-surface history to hand over with it. This function makes the folders that history will live in."
    },
    {
      "file": "bin/init.mjs",
      "line": 102,
      "pattern": "await mkdir\\(cl\\);",
      "title": "Reserve a new index; preserve an existing one",
      "description": "Nonrecursive mkdir reserves a new CHANGELOG directory. An existing directory produces a no-op with exit 0; that does not validate its contents or wait for another process to finish.\n\nA second run must preserve real history. A partially present category layout is still usable because add creates the directory it needs."
    },
    {
      "file": "bin/init.mjs",
      "line": 40,
      "pattern": "const CATEGORIES = \\[",
      "title": "The domain vocabulary, declared once",
      "description": "Six kinds of surface a change can touch. This one array is simultaneously a set of directory names, the valid values of the `add` command's first argument, and a line of help text.\n\nBefore the wave-3 pass those six words were written out in four separate places. Collapsing them to one constant is why a seventh category is now a one-line change."
    },
    {
      "file": "bin/init.mjs",
      "line": 113,
      "pattern": "for \\(const sub of CATEGORIES\\)",
      "title": "Six directories from the one list",
      "description": "The lane directories are created straight from CATEGORIES, so the folder layout can never disagree with what `add` accepts.\n\nFive of the six will be empty, and git does not track empty directories. That is the fact behind defect D1 — and the reason the fix went into `add` rather than here."
    },
    {
      "file": "bin/init.mjs",
      "line": 118,
      "pattern": "CHANGELOG-README\\.md",
      "title": "Two files copied, not generated",
      "description": "The master index and the format spec are copied verbatim out of `templates/`. Nothing in `templates/` is ever imported — every file there is data."
    },
    {
      "file": "templates/CHANGELOG-README.md",
      "line": 1,
      "pattern": "per-surface changelog index",
      "title": "What the adopter opens first",
      "description": "This becomes `CHANGELOG/README.md` in their repo. Line 1 used to read `# SitFlow — per-surface changelog index` and 83 of its rows named another product's routes — a stranger's finished index, landing on day one. It is now a skeleton they fill in."
    },
    {
      "file": "bin/init.mjs",
      "line": 149,
      "pattern": "!CATEGORIES\\.includes\\(category\\)",
      "title": "Validation is a gate, not a transform",
      "description": "`add widgets Thing` stops here. The error lists all six valid values, so the user never has to leave the terminal to find them — that shape is a convention worth keeping in any new error message."
    },
    {
      "file": "bin/init.mjs",
      "line": 167,
      "pattern": "await mkdir\\(dir, \\{ recursive: true \\}\\);",
      "title": "Defect D1 died on this line",
      "description": "One line, replacing a five-line guard that exited 1 when the lane directory was missing.\n\nThe person who runs `init` gets six lane directories; five stay empty; git tracks none of the empty ones; so the second person to clone the repo has one lane directory, not six. They ran `add`, got `✗ CHANGELOG\\pages does not exist`, were told to run `init`, and `init` declined because `CHANGELOG/` existed. A closed loop, at the second person, on the product's headline claim.\n\nTwo fixes were written down: write a `.gitkeep` into each lane directory, or let `add` make the directory it needs. This is the second — it removes a code path instead of adding six files."
    },
    {
      "file": "bin/init.mjs",
      "line": 179,
      "pattern": "await writeFile\\(target, personalized, \\{ flag: \"wx\" \\}\\);",
      "title": "Never overwrite a lane",
      "description": "Exclusive file creation reserves a new lane. If the destination exists, the invocation refuses with a nonzero exit and preserves its bytes.\n\nThe four-creator scenario checks one writer succeeds and the other three refuse, followed by eight later lane creations that preserve the original lane and packet."
    },
    {
      "file": "bin/init.mjs",
      "line": 172,
      "pattern": "readFile\\(join\\(TPL_DIR, \"lane\\.md\"\\)",
      "title": "Personalize a fresh lane without inventing history",
      "description": "Read the lane template, personalize the surface and current date, and create the new file exclusively. The current entry remains unfilled and unavailable commit/author facts stay pending. The instructional example stays fenced; existing history is never regenerated."
    },
    {
      "file": "templates/lane.md",
      "line": 7,
      "pattern": "^## YYYY-MM-DD — Pending — describe this change",
      "title": "Replace apparent sample history with pending facts",
      "description": "The original D7 output carried sample entries and a fake commit outside the instructional example. A new lane now leaves current facts visibly unfilled and keeps a single fenced format example.\n\nThe old observed failure remains in promotion history. The current scenario must reject invented history, rather than preserve the old bad expectation."
    },
    {
      "file": "bin/init.mjs",
      "line": 365,
      "pattern": "\\} catch \\(e\\) \\{",
      "title": "No stack traces, ever",
      "description": "The outermost catch turns unexpected filesystem failures into a concise error. A nonzero exit means the requested operation did not finish; it can still have created new files before a conflict.\n\nThere is no automatic rollback or retry. Preserve existing content, identify the conflicting destination, and do not print Installed after a failed install."
    },
    {
      "file": "promotion/PROMOTION_LOG.md",
      "line": 108,
      "pattern": "^\\| D1 \\|",
      "title": "The defect this walkthrough kept mentioning",
      "description": "This row preserves the original D1 reproduction: Git omitted empty directories and the second developer was told to run an init command that declined. Later repairs must not rewrite that observation.\n\nRead current CONCERNS.md and the current scenario receipts alongside this historical ledger; the ledger does not automatically acquire later repair status."
    },
    {
      "file": "test/cli.test.mjs",
      "line": 201,
      "pattern": "J1 init scaffolds the six lanes",
      "title": "What proves all of the above",
      "description": "Scenario tests run the real CLI in owned temporary directories and assert process results plus actual files. Preservation checks include conflicting edits, duplicate writers, and finite accumulation.\n\nThe original help-only test could not reject bad behavior. The current tour and citation guards must also keep their anchors aligned to the final source."
    }
  ]
}
